|passage=Contending for principles of the '''last''' importance.}}
# Lowest in rank or degree.
#: {{ux|en|Three contestants will win awards, but the '''last''' prize is just a book voucher.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1797|author=w:Richard Cumberland|title=w:The Last of the Family|title2=The Posthumous Dramatick Words of the Late Richard Cumberland, Esq.|volume2=2|year2=1813|page2=237|pageurl2=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=Sv1DAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA237|text=I will not wish you to consider me but as the '''last''' and lowest of mankind.}}
