====Determiner====
{{en-det}}

# The (one) immediately before the present.
#: {{ux|en|We went there '''last''' year.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was '''last''' to arrive.}}
# {{lb|en|of days of the week or months of the year}} Closest in the [[past]], or closest but one if the closest was very recent; of days, sometimes thought to specifically refer to the instance closest to seven days (one week) ago, or the most recent instance ''before'' seven days (one week) ago.
#: {{ux|en|It's Wednesday, and the party was '''last''' Tuesday; that is, not yesterday, but eight days ago.}}
#: {{ux|en|When you say '''last''' Monday, do you mean the Monday just gone, or the one before that?}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|both senses}} This cannot be used in past or future tense to refer to a time immediately before the subject matter. For example, one does not say {{m|en||I was very tired yesterday, due to not having slept well last night}}: {{m|en||last night}} in that sentence refers to the night before the speaker is speaking, not the night before the "yesterday" to which he refers. He would need to say {{m|en||I was very tired yesterday, due to not having slept well the night before}} or the like.

